course: dictionary
lesson: 11997
title: Characterisation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Characterisation is the way a writer shows what a character is like. Writers rarely say "Mia is kind." Instead, they show it. «Mia gave her last sandwich to the new girl who had forgot her lunch.» We learn Mia is kind because of what she does.
explain: Writers show characters in four main ways: through what they say, what they do, what they think, and how other people react to them. «"Let me help you," Mia said softly.» Her words tell us she is caring. When her friends smile at her, we learn that others like her too.
explain: In English lessons, you might be asked to comment on a writer's characterisation. Find the clues, then explain what they show. Ask yourself: what does this character do or say, and what does that tell me about them? Then write your answer in your own words, using a quote as proof.
fact: Characterisation means the way a writer or actor shows what a character is like.
fact: «Characterisation» is spelled «characterization» in American English.
fact: A writer can show characterisation through speech, actions, thoughts and how other characters react.
fact: In a formal sense, characterisation is a description of the main qualities of someone or something.
fact: In science, the characterisation of a material describes its properties, such as how hard or heavy it is.
exercise: «The writer shows Ben is greedy when he grabs the last cake without asking.» Which word means the way a writer shows what a character is like? | Scenery | Rhythm | Punctuation | *Characterisation
exercise: «"Please, let me go first," said Nadia, stepping back to let the little ones pass.» What does this line show about Nadia? | She is the tallest in class | *She is polite and thoughtful | She is lost | She is angry about the queue
exercise: «The report gave a clear characterisation of the new bridge, its strength and its materials.» What does characterisation mean here? | A kind of paint | A bridge that falls down | A short poem about bridges | *A description of the main qualities of something
test: «The author's characterisation of the king shows he is proud and never listens.» What does characterisation mean in this sentence? | A type of cloud | *The way the writer shows what the king is like | A map of the castle | A list of the king's dinners
test: Which example shows characterisation through a character's actions? | There were three chapters in the book | The sun was yellow and the sky was blue | *Ella gives her lunch to a hungry friend, so we learn she is generous | The book had two hundred pages
exam: «Rex was always late, forgot his books and laughed when the teacher was upset.» What does the writer's characterisation tell us about Rex? | That the school is by the sea | *That Rex is careless and disrespectful | That Rex lives on a farm | That the book is very long
